d9\\/w682\\/q80\\/wpoJPG\\/cx110\\/cw554\\/ch553\\/images\\/uploads\\/635e7580c03f13f27d14da28a391f7d9.webp 1210w\",\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/63\\/5e7580c03f13f27d14da28a391f7d9\\/w682\\/q80\\/wpoJPG\\/cx110\\/cw554\\/ch553\\/images\\/uploads\\/635e7580c03f13f27d14da28a391f7d9.webp 1470w\",\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/63\\/5e7580c03f13f27d14da28a391f7d9\\/w682\\/q80\\/wpoJPG\\/cx110\\/cw554\\/ch553\\/images\\/uploads\\/635e7580c03f13f27d14da28a391f7d9.webp 1680w\",\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/63\\/5e7580c03f13f27d14da28a391f7d9\\/w682\\/q80\\/wpoJPG\\/cx110\\/cw554\\/ch553\\/images\\/uploads\\/635e7580c03f13f27d14da28a391f7d9.webp 1870w\",\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/63\\/5e7580c03f13f27d14da28a391f7d9\\/w682\\/q80\\/wpoJPG\\/cx110\\/cw554\\/ch553\\/images\\/uploads\\/635e7580c03f13f27d14da28a391f7d9.webp 2048w\",\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/63\\/5e7580c03f13f27d14da28a391f7d9\\/w682\\/q80\\/wpoJPG\\/cx110\\/cw554\\/ch553\\/images\\/uploads\\/635e7580c03f13f27d14da28a391f7d9.webp 2880w\"],\"focal_point\":\"\",\"search_text\":\"Proudly presented as part of our MADE AT RIVERSIDE TV strand; celebrating the long history of film and TV production at Riverside Studios. Here we continue our longstanding celebration of the inimitable Tony Hancock, with a further three episodes of Hancock's classic work. The Tony Hancock Appreciation Society will introduce and discuss the episode afterwards as usual.\\u00a0Episodes:Hancock's Half Hour: The New Nose (Made at Riverside)Hancock (1963 ATV Series): The Eye WitnessHancock: The Bedsitter\\u00a0With thanks to our collaborators on this event, the Tony Hancock Appreciation Society, the estates of writers Ray Galton and Alan Simpson, the estate of Tony Hancock, and the British Film Institute.\",\"book_link\":\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/seats\\/15060\\/\",\"event_type\":[\"101\"],\"event_age_ratings\":[\"81002\"],\"search\":\"Hancock XI Hancock XI Cinema  <p>Proudly presented as part of our <strong>MADE AT RIVERSIDE TV<\\/strong> strand; celebrating the long history of film and TV production at Riverside Studios. Here we continue our longstanding celebration of the inimitable Tony Hancock, with a further three episodes of Hancock's classic work.<strong> The Tony Hancock Appreciation Society<\\/strong> will introduce and discuss the episode afterwards as usual.<\\/p><p>&nbsp;<\\/p><p>Episodes:<\\/p><p><i>Hancock's Half Hour: The New Nose (Made at Riverside)<\\/i><\\/p><p><i>Hancock (1963 ATV Series): The Eye Witness<\\/i><\\/p><p><i>Hancock: The Bedsitter<\\/i><\\/p><p>&nbsp;<\\/p><p>With thanks to our collaborators on this event, the <strong>Tony Hancock Appreciation Society,<\\/strong> the estates of writers Ray Galton and Alan Simpson, the estate of Tony Hancock, and the British Film Institute.<\\/p> Hancock's Half Hour Triple Bill: Part XI,Hancock XI  Proudly presented as part of our MADE AT RIVERSIDE TV strand; celebrating the long history of film and TV production at Riverside Studios. Here we continue our longstanding celebration of the inimitable Tony Hancock, with a further three episodes of Hancock's classic work. The Tony Hancock Appreciation Society will introduce and discuss the episode afterwards as usual.\\u00a0Episodes:Hancock's Half Hour: The New Nose (Made at Riverside)Hancock (1963 ATV Series): The Eye WitnessHancock: The Bedsitter\\u00a0With thanks to our collaborators on this event, the Tony Hancock Appreciation Society, the estates of writers Ray Galton and Alan Simpson, the estate of Tony Hancock, and the British Film Institute. Cinema PG\"},{\"url\":\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/whats-on\\/gv-bossa-nova-night-a-tribute-to-joao-gilberto-by-mario-bakuna\\/\",\"id\":\"965\",\"name\":\"Bossa Nova Night: A Tribute to Jo\\u00e3o Gilberto by Mario Bakuna\",\"title\":\"Bossa Nova Night: A Tribute to Jo\\u00e3o Gilberto by Mario Bakuna\",\"duration\":\"90 minutes\",\"slot_tag\":\"Music\",\"link_title\":\"More Info\",\"performances\":{\"1769817600\":[{\"tag_ids\":[\"113\"],\"tag_name\":\"\",\"html\":\"<a class=\\\"performance button\\\" href=\\\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/seats\\/30802\\/\\\">\\n   \\n      <div class=\\\"performance-time\\\" data-acc=\\\"\\\">19:30<\\/div>\\n    \\n<\\/a>\\n\",\"timestamp\":\"1769887800\",\"accessibility_class\":\"\"}]},\"performance_dates\":[1769817600],\"start_date\":\"1769887800\",\"end_date\":\"1769887800\",\"age_rating_class\":\"\",\"ticket_free\":false,\"priority_booking\":true,\"hash\":\"cUduTEFRRnRaNzFXbGs0Rzg1eGxydz09\",\"embed_id\":\"\",\"embed_host\":\"\",\"date_formatted\":\"Sat 31 Jan 2026\",\"text\":\"Featuring Mario Bakuna on Acoustic Guitar and VocalsFollowing sold-out performances across the UK, Portugal, France, Spain, and the Netherlands, Mario&hellip;\",\"image_url\":\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/5e\\/d3c152ad1dcfd8c0c199f6ffb17975\\/w880\\/q80\\/cx1359\\/cy33\\/cw3305\\/ch3300\\/images\\/uploads\\/5ed3c152ad1dcfd8c0c199f6ffb17975.jpg\",\"image_source\":\"type=\\\"image\\/webp\\\" srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/5e\\/d3c152ad1dcfd8c0c199f6ffb17975\\/w880\\/q80\\/wpojpg\\/cx1359\\/cy33\\/cw3305\\/ch3300\\/images\\/uploads\\/5ed3c152ad1dcfd8c0c199f6ffb17975.webp 880w,https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/5e\\/d3c152ad1dcfd8c0c199f6ffb17975\\/w1210\\/q80\\/wpojpg\\/cx1359\\/cy33\\/cw3305\\/ch3300\\/images\\/uploads\\/5ed3c152ad1dcfd8c0c199f6ffb17975.webp 1210w,https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/5e\\/d3c152ad1dcfd8c0c199f6ffb17975\\/w1470\\/q80\\/wpojpg\\/cx1359\\/cy33\\/cw3305\\/ch3300\\/images\\/uploads\\/5ed3c152ad1dcfd8c0c199f6ffb17975.webp 1470w,https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/5e\\/d3c152ad1dcfd8c0c199f6ffb17975\\/w1680\\/q80\\/wpojpg\\/cx1359\\/cy33\\/cw3305\\/ch3300\\/images\\/uploads\\/5ed3c152ad1dcfd8c0c199f6ffb17975.webp 1680w,https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/5e\\/d3c152ad1dcfd8c0c199f6ffb17975\\/w1870\\/q80\\/wpojpg\\/cx1359\\/cy33\\/cw3305\\/ch3300\\/images\\/uploads\\/5ed3c152ad1dcfd8c0c199f6ffb17975.webp 1870w,https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/5e\\/d3c152ad1dcfd8c0c199f6ffb17975\\/w2048\\/q80\\/wpojpg\\/cx1359\\/cy33\\/cw3305\\/ch3300\\/images\\/uploads\\/5ed3c152ad1dcfd8c0c199f6ffb17975.webp 2048w,https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/5e\\/d3c152ad1dcfd8c0c199f6ffb17975\\/w2880\\/q80\\/wpojpg\\/cx1359\\/cy33\\/cw3305\\/ch3300\\/images\\/uploads\\/5ed3c152ad1dcfd8c0c199f6ffb17975.webp 2880w\\\"\",\"image_alt\":\"\",\"image_cap\":\"\",\"image_data\":[\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/5e\\/d3c152ad1dcfd8c0c199f6ffb17975\\/w880\\/q80\\/wpojpg\\/cx1359\\/cy33\\/cw3305\\/ch3300\\/images\\/uploads\\/5ed3c152ad1dcfd8c0c199f6ffb17975.webp 880w\",\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/5e\\/d3c152ad1dcfd8c0c199f6ffb17975\\/w1210\\/q80\\/wpojpg\\/cx1359\\/cy33\\/cw3305\\/ch3300\\/images\\/uploads\\/5ed3c152ad1dcfd8c0c199f6ffb17975.webp 1210w\",\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/5e\\/d3c152ad1dcfd8c0c199f6ffb17975\\/w1470\\/q80\\/wpojpg\\/cx1359\\/cy33\\/cw3305\\/ch3300\\/images\\/uploads\\/5ed3c152ad1dcfd8c0c199f6ffb17975.webp 1470w\",\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/5e\\/d3c152ad1dcfd8c0c199f6ffb17975\\/w1680\\/q80\\/wpojpg\\/cx1359\\/cy33\\/cw3305\\/ch3300\\/images\\/uploads\\/5ed3c152ad1dcfd8c0c199f6ffb17975.webp 1680w\",\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/5e\\/d3c152ad1dcfd8c0c199f6ffb17975\\/w1870\\/q80\\/wpojpg\\/cx1359\\/cy33\\/cw3305\\/ch3300\\/images\\/uploads\\/5ed3c152ad1dcfd8c0c199f6ffb17975.webp 1870w\",\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/5e\\/d3c152ad1dcfd8c0c199f6ffb17975\\/w2048\\/q80\\/wpojpg\\/cx1359\\/cy33\\/cw3305\\/ch3300\\/images\\/uploads\\/5ed3c152ad1dcfd8c0c199f6ffb17975.webp 2048w\",\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/5e\\/d3c152ad1dcfd8c0c199f6ffb17975\\/w2880\\/q80\\/wpojpg\\/cx1359\\/cy33\\/cw3305\\/ch3300\\/images\\/uploads\\/5ed3c152ad1dcfd8c0c199f6ffb17975.webp 2880w\"],\"focal_point\":\"\",\"search_text\":\"Featuring Mario Bakuna on Acoustic Guitar and VocalsFollowing sold-out performances across the UK, Portugal, France, Spain, and the Netherlands, Mario Bakuna is delighted to bring this special concert to the Riverside Studios.Join him in celebrating the legacy of Jo\\u00e3o Gilberto, the legendary Brazilian musician and pioneering father of Bossa Nova in the late 1950s. In this heartfelt tribute, Mario Bakuna presents reinterpretations of Gilberto\\u2019s work alongside his own original compositions. Audiences can expect a rich blend of traditional samba elements, syncopated rhythms of plucked chords, and the breezy sophistication that defines Bossa Nova.\\u00a0Mario Bakuna is a Brazilian composer, arranger, vocalist, and guitarist with over 20 years of professional experience, currently based in London, UK. Well known for his deep exploration of traditional Brazilian rhythms, samba, jazz, and bossa nova, Mario focuses on both original compositions and fresh arrangements of works by iconic artists like Tom Jobim, Dorival Caymmi, Paulo Moura, and Jo\\u00e3o Donato. In recent years, he has also dedicated his research and performance to reinterpreting Samba Jazz, a genre that emerged in 1950s Rio de Janeiro through the work of artists like Luiz E\\u00e7a, Tamba Trio, and Edson Machado. This style blends Brazilian standards with sophisticated harmonies influenced by the post\\u2013bossa nova movement.Driven by a passion for musical exploration, Mario moved to Europe to deepen his research and expand his artistic horizons. Since settling in London, he has collaborated with artists such as Jean Toussaint, Liam Noble, Ricardo dos Santos, Edmundo Carneiro, Cacau Queiroz, Alain Jean-Marie, Dudu Penz, and Fil\\u00f3 Machado. He has since become a prominent figure and key reference in the UK\\u2019s Brazilian jazz scene, performing extensively across Europe and beyond at renowned venues and international festivals.His albums Where Rio de Janeiro Meets Bahia and Brazilian Landscapes highlight his ability to fuse traditional roots with a contemporary musical sensibility. With sold-out concerts and critical acclaim, these projects have toured across 20 European countries, as well as Brazil, Canada, Madagascar, Egypt, Kazakhstan, and Azerbaijan\\u2014captivating audiences around the world.\\u00a0\\u201cMario Bakuna, a sparkling guitarist, plays with palpable feeling - his virtuosic fluency on the fretboard is controlled and flourishes are perfectly placed. His voice has a texture like heavy cloth\\u201d. (Songlines Magazine)\\u201cMario Bakuna, a man who exudes music. (\\u2026) \\u2018vocals\\u2019 doesn\\u2019t begin to do him justice: his expressive range and the precision with which he was able to deploy it was truly the band\\u2019s fifth instrument. \\u00a0(\\u2026) And he did this while playing guitar with precision and finesse. (\\u2026) his solos were a further source of amazement, his technique somewhere between finger-picking style and classical. His solo introduction to a Baden Powell number made a hash of any attempt at a definition.\\u201d (The Whitman Review, Wakefield Jazz)\\u00a0Website: https:\\/\\/www.mariobakuna.comFacebook: https:\\/\\/www.facebook.com\\/MarioBakunaMusicianInstagram: https:\\/\\/www.instagram.com\\/mariobakunaYouTube: https:\\/\\/www.youtube.com\\/c\\/mariobakunaListen:\\u00a0https:\\/\\/mariobakuna.bandcamp.com\\u00a0Video sample:\\u00a0https:\\/\\/www.youtube.com\\/watch?v=i8f5jxuzASE\",\"book_link\":\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/seats\\/30802\\/\",\"event_type\":[\"113\"],\"search\":\"Bossa Nova Night: A Tribute to Jo\\u00e3o Gilberto by Mario Bakuna Bossa Nova Night: A Tribute to Jo\\u00e3o Gilberto by Mario Bakuna Music  <p><i>Featuring Mario Bakuna on Acoustic Guitar and Vocals<\\/i><\\/p><p>Following sold-out performances across the UK, Portugal, France, Spain, and the Netherlands, Mario Bakuna is delighted to bring this special concert to the Riverside Studios.<\\/p><p>Join him in celebrating the legacy of Jo\\u00e3o Gilberto, the legendary Brazilian musician and pioneering father of Bossa Nova in the late 1950s. In this heartfelt tribute, Mario Bakuna presents reinterpretations of Gilberto\\u2019s work alongside his own original compositions. Audiences can expect a rich blend of traditional samba elements, syncopated rhythms of plucked chords, and the breezy sophistication that defines Bossa Nova.<\\/p><p>&nbsp;<\\/p><p><strong>Mario Bakuna<\\/strong> is a Brazilian composer, arranger, vocalist, and guitarist with over 20 years of professional experience, currently based in London, UK. Well known for his deep exploration of traditional Brazilian rhythms, samba, jazz, and bossa nova, Mario focuses on both original compositions and fresh arrangements of works by iconic artists like Tom Jobim, Dorival Caymmi, Paulo Moura, and Jo\\u00e3o Donato. In recent years, he has also dedicated his research and performance to reinterpreting Samba Jazz, a genre that emerged in 1950s Rio de Janeiro through the work of artists like Luiz E\\u00e7a, Tamba Trio, and Edson Machado. This style blends Brazilian standards with sophisticated harmonies influenced by the post\\u2013bossa nova movement.<\\/p><p>Driven by a passion for musical exploration, Mario moved to Europe to deepen his research and expand his artistic horizons. Since settling in London, he has collaborated with artists such as Jean Toussaint, Liam Noble, Ricardo dos Santos, Edmundo Carneiro, Cacau Queiroz, Alain Jean-Marie, Dudu Penz, and Fil\\u00f3 Machado. He has since become a prominent figure and key reference in the UK\\u2019s Brazilian jazz scene, performing extensively across Europe and beyond at renowned venues and international festivals.<\\/p><p>His albums <i>Where Rio de Janeiro Meets Bahia<\\/i> and <i>Brazilian Landscapes<\\/i> highlight his ability to fuse traditional roots with a contemporary musical sensibility. With sold-out concerts and critical acclaim, these projects have toured across 20 European countries, as well as Brazil, Canada, Madagascar, Egypt, Kazakhstan, and Azerbaijan\\u2014captivating audiences around the world.<\\/p><p>&nbsp;<\\/p><p>\\u201c<i>Mario Bakuna, a sparkling guitarist, plays with palpable feeling - his virtuosic fluency on the fretboard is controlled and flourishes are perfectly placed. His voice has a texture like heavy cloth\\u201d. (Songlines Magazine)<\\/i><\\/p><p><i>\\u201cMario Bakuna, a man who exudes music. (\\u2026) \\u2018vocals\\u2019 doesn\\u2019t begin to do him justice: his expressive range and the precision with which he was able to deploy it was truly the band\\u2019s fifth instrument. &nbsp;(\\u2026) And he did this while playing guitar with precision and finesse. (\\u2026) his solos were a further source of amazement, his technique somewhere between finger-picking style and classical. His solo introduction to a Baden Powell number made a hash of any attempt at a definition.\\u201d (The Whitman Review, Wakefield Jazz)<\\/i><\\/p><p>&nbsp;<\\/p><p>Website: <a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.mariobakuna.com\\/\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\">https:\\/\\/www.mariobakuna.com<\\/a><\\/p><p>Facebook: <a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.facebook.com\\/MarioBakunaMusician\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\">https:\\/\\/www.facebook.com\\/MarioBakunaMusician<\\/a><\\/p><p>Instagram: <a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.instagram.com\\/mariobakuna\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\">https:\\/\\/www.instagram.com\\/mariobakuna<\\/a><\\/p><p>YouTube: <a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.youtube.com\\/c\\/mariobakuna\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\">https:\\/\\/www.youtube.com\\/c\\/mariobakuna<\\/a><\\/p><p>Listen:&nbsp;<a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/mariobakuna.bandcamp.com\\/\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\">https:\\/\\/mariobakuna.bandcamp.com<\\/a><\\/p><p>&nbsp;<\\/p><p>Video sample:&nbsp;<a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.youtube.com\\/watch?v=i8f5jxuzASE\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\">https:\\/\\/www.youtube.com\\/watch?v=i8f5jxuzASE<\\/a><\\/p> Bossa Nova Night: A Tribute to Jo\\u00e3o Gilberto by Mario Bakuna  Featuring Mario Bakuna on Acoustic Guitar and VocalsFollowing sold-out performances across the UK, Portugal, France, Spain, and the Netherlands, Mario Bakuna is delighted to bring this special concert to the Riverside Studios.Join him in celebrating the legacy of Jo\\u00e3o Gilberto, the legendary Brazilian musician and pioneering father of Bossa Nova in the late 1950s. In this heartfelt tribute, Mario Bakuna presents reinterpretations of Gilberto\\u2019s work alongside his own original compositions. Audiences can expect a rich blend of traditional samba elements, syncopated rhythms of plucked chords, and the breezy sophistication that defines Bossa Nova.\\u00a0Mario Bakuna is a Brazilian composer, arranger, vocalist, and guitarist with over 20 years of professional experience, currently based in London, UK. Well known for his deep exploration of traditional Brazilian rhythms, samba, jazz, and bossa nova, Mario focuses on both original compositions and fresh arrangements of works by iconic artists like Tom Jobim, Dorival Caymmi, Paulo Moura, and Jo\\u00e3o Donato. In recent years, he has also dedicated his research and performance to reinterpreting Samba Jazz, a genre that emerged in 1950s Rio de Janeiro through the work of artists like Luiz E\\u00e7a, Tamba Trio, and Edson Machado. This style blends Brazilian standards with sophisticated harmonies influenced by the post\\u2013bossa nova movement.Driven by a passion for musical exploration, Mario moved to Europe to deepen his research and expand his artistic horizons. Since settling in London, he has collaborated with artists such as Jean Toussaint, Liam Noble, Ricardo dos Santos, Edmundo Carneiro, Cacau Queiroz, Alain Jean-Marie, Dudu Penz, and Fil\\u00f3 Machado. He has since become a prominent figure and key reference in the UK\\u2019s Brazilian jazz scene, performing extensively across Europe and beyond at renowned venues and international festivals.His albums Where Rio de Janeiro Meets Bahia and Brazilian Landscapes highlight his ability to fuse traditional roots with a contemporary musical sensibility. With sold-out concerts and critical acclaim, these projects have toured across 20 European countries, as well as Brazil, Canada, Madagascar, Egypt, Kazakhstan, and Azerbaijan\\u2014captivating audiences around the world.\\u00a0\\u201cMario Bakuna, a sparkling guitarist, plays with palpable feeling - his virtuosic fluency on the fretboard is controlled and flourishes are perfectly placed. His voice has a texture like heavy cloth\\u201d. (Songlines Magazine)\\u201cMario Bakuna, a man who exudes music. (\\u2026) \\u2018vocals\\u2019 doesn\\u2019t begin to do him justice: his expressive range and the precision with which he was able to deploy it was truly the band\\u2019s fifth instrument. \\u00a0(\\u2026) And he did this while playing guitar with precision and finesse. (\\u2026) his solos were a further source of amazement, his technique somewhere between finger-picking style and classical. His solo introduction to a Baden Powell number made a hash of any attempt at a definition.\\u201d (The Whitman Review, Wakefield Jazz)\\u00a0Website: https:\\/\\/www.mariobakuna.comFacebook: https:\\/\\/www.facebook.com\\/MarioBakunaMusicianInstagram: https:\\/\\/www.instagram.com\\/mariobakunaYouTube: https:\\/\\/www.youtube.com\\/c\\/mariobakunaListen:\\u00a0https:\\/\\/mariobakuna.bandcamp.com\\u00a0Video sample:\\u00a0https:\\/\\/www.youtube.com\\/watch?v=i8f5jxuzASE Music\"},{\"url\":\"https:\\/\\/riv