            "text": "<!DOCTYPE html>\n\n\n<html lang=\"en\" class=\"no-js\">\n\n<head>\n  <title>London Short Film Festival Showcase: Palestine Looks Back | Riverside Studios</title>\n\n    <meta name=\"description\" content=\"Palestinian voices who dared to go beyond what was asked, turning their gaze back on the West - its inaction, border regimes, colonial history, but also its solidarity and environment.This programme is curated by Theo Panagopoulos. The Goodness Regime, di\">\n    \n<meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n\n<meta name=\"generator\" content=\"Grandad Digital - Powered by You.Create Content Management System\">\n<meta http-equiv=\"X-UA-Compatible\" content=\"IE=Edge\">\n\n<script type=\"application/ld+json\">\n{\n  \"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n  \"@type\": \"Organization\",\n  \"url\": \"https://riversidestudios.co.uk/\",\n  \"logo\": \"https://riversidestudios.co.uk/assets/img/logo.png\"\n}\n</script>\n<script type=\"application/ld+json\">{\"@context\":\"https:\\/\\/schema.org\",\"@type\":\"Event\",\"name\":\"London Short Film Festival Showcase: Palestine Looks Back\",\"description\":\"Palestinian voices who dared to go beyond what was asked, turning their gaze back on the West - its inaction, border regimes, colonial history, but also its solidarity and environment.This programme is curated by Theo Panagopoulos.&nbsp;The Goodness Regime, dir. Jumana Manna and Sille Storihle, Norway \\/ Palestine 2013, 20minsIt's a long way from Amphioxus, dir. Kamal Aljafari, Germany 2019, 16minsNachbarn (Neighbours), dir. Pary El-Qalqili and Christiane Schmidt, Germany 2018, 26 minsElefsina Notre Amour, dir. Mahdi Fleifel, Greece 2023, 9minsThey Live in Forests, They are Extremely Shy, dir. Saeed Taji Farouky, UK 2016, 4minsWe began by measuring distance, dir. Basma Alsharif, Egypt 2009, 19mins&nbsp;Contains themes of death and injury.\",\"image\":[\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/uploads\\/0c3fbe83ebdbd5a58b891a5913633970.jpg\"],\"startDate\":\"202